{"api_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/19493","collected_at":"2026-09-27T21:56:24.566372+00:00","comments":[{"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"Hello!\r\n\r\nThe Cloud TPU v5p chip contains 2 tensorcores and 4 sparsecores as mentioned in the doc: https://cloud.google.com/tpu/docs/v5p-training#system-architecture\r\n\r\nOn a v5p-8 machine, I would imagine that 8 refers to the number of tensorcores on that machines. Here, JAX talks to 4 TPU devices/chips, essentially 2x2x1 (https://cloud.google.com/tpu/docs/v5p-training#v5p_tpu_configurations) = 4 but not every single TensorCores.\r\n\r\nIf you run `jax.device_count()`, it should return 4 instead of the number of tensorcores of a v5p-8 machine. You should define your mesh/sharding based on the actual device number.","created_at":"2024-01-24T22:40:33Z","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/19493#issuecomment-1909039597","id":1909039597,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/19493","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5xyaHt","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1909039597/reactions"},"updated_at":"2024-01-24T22:40:33Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1909039597","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9438093?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yliu120","id":9438093,"login":"yliu120","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk0MzgwOTM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yliu120/rec